## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical ability to design an end-to-end, event-driven image analytics pipeline in AWS using beginner-friendly services (S3, Lambda, Rekognition, DynamoDB) with real-world concerns like privacy, cost, and tenancy.

## Key Concepts
- Event-driven flow triggered by S3 PUT
- Rekognition detectLabels with top N labels
- Lightweight color palette extraction in Lambda
- Descriptor JSON stored in S3 and DynamoDB upsert
- IAM least privilege, DLQ/backoff, cost awareness

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js Lambda pseudo
const rek = new AWS.Rekognition();
const s3 = new AWS.S3();
const ddb = new AWS.DynamoDB.DocumentClient();

exports.handler = async (evt) => {
  const key = evt.Records[0].s3.object.key;
  const bucket = evt.Records[0].s3.bucket.name;
  const img = await s3.getObject({Bucket:bucket,Key:key}).promise();
  const labels = await rek.detectLabels({Image:{Bytes: img.Body}, MaxLabels:3, MinConfidence: 60}).promise();
  const colors = extractColors(img.Body); // simple utility
  const descriptor = { imageKey:key, labels: labels.Labels.map(l=>l.Name), colors, timestamp: Date.now(), facesDetected: labels.Labels.some(l=>l.Name==='Face') };
  await s3.putObject({Bucket: bucket, Key: key + '.json', Body: JSON.stringify(descriptor)}).promise();
  await ddb.update({TableName:'ProductImages',Key:{productId: determineProductId(key)}, UpdateExpression:'SET labels=:l, colors=:c, imageKey=:k, privacyFlag=:p', ExpressionAttributeValues:{':l':descriptor.labels, ':c':descriptor.colors, ':k':key, ':p':false}}).promise();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate labels and handle false positives? 
- How would you extend for multi-tenant isolation and cost controls?
